   "evidence": "Peskin\u2013Schroeder's trace identity tr[\u03b3^\u03bc\u03b3^\u03bd\u03b3^\u03c1\u03b3^\u03c3\u03b3^5] = -4i \u03b5^{\u03bc\u03bd\u03c1\u03c3} with \u03b3^5 = i\u03b3^0\u03b3^1\u03b3^2\u03b3^3 gives tr[\u03b3^0\u03b3^1\u03b3^2\u03b3^3\u03b3^5] = i tr((\u03b3^0\u03b3^1\u03b3^2\u03b3^3)^2) = -4i, hence \u03b5^{0123} = +1 in their convention. The roadmap's own convention line also fixes `\u03b5\u2070\u00b9\u00b2\u00b3 = +1` (roadmap/EpsilonEridaniRoadmaps/MultiPartonCorrelations/README.md:141), consistent with P&S and not with the cited sign.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Tensors/RealTensor/Vector/VolumeForm.lean",
   "fix": "Either re-cite the convention to a source that actually uses `\u03b5_{0123} = +1` (e.g. Bjorken\u2013Drell), or keep Peskin\u2013Schroeder and state that this file's `volumeForm` is the negative of their `\u03b5^{\u03bc\u03bd\u03c1\u03c3}`.",
   "issue": "The module docstring (line 18-19) and References entry (line 43-44) credit Peskin\u2013Schroeder for the convention `\u03b5^{0123} = -1` (i.e. `\u03b5_{0123} = +1`). Peskin\u2013Schroeder use `\u03b5^{0123} = +1`; the `\u03b5_{0123} = +1` convention is Bjorken\u2013Drell's. The citation points a reader to a source that states the opposite sign.",
   "line": 18
